    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the driveway so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the access point at night or in low-visibility conditions.\n• Designate and keep clear a flat, firm area near the main residence where emergency vehicles can turn around without backing long distances.\n• Keep the full width of the access drive clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and overgrown vegetation so emergency vehicles can reach both structures.\n• Post visible address or unit identifiers on both the main residence and the detached structure so responders can distinguish between buildings on arrival.\n• Clear a direct walking path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings without navigating around obstacles.\n• Keep gates along the access drive unlocked or secured with a Knox-style lock box so responders are not delayed at a barrier during an emergency.\n• Trim any vegetation along the access drive that reduces the usable width or overhead clearance for emergency vehicles.\n• Identify and communicate the single access point limitation to your local fire station so they are aware that all response vehicles must enter and exit the same way."
